WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.478
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:15.658
Unit thirty: Have to / Don't have to. Today you will talk about rules and things that are not necessary.

4
00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:18.610
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.637
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.461
Have to.

7
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.751
Have to means to be obliged to do something.

8
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.966
I have to wear a uniform.

9
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.005
Your turn. Say: Have to.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:36.937
Have to.

11
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:38.731
Has to.

12
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:42.900
Has to means he, she or it is obliged to do something.

13
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:45.110
She has to get up early.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.765
Your turn. Say: Has to.

15
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.427
Has to.

16
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:53.324
Don't have to.

17
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.303
Don't have to means it is not necessary to do something.

18
00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:59.394
You don't have to pay.

19
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:02.496
Your turn. Say: Don't have to.

20
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:06.439
Don't have to.

21
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:08.451
Doesn't have to.

22
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.669
Doesn't have to means it is not necessary for him, her or it.

23
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:14.702
He doesn't have to come.

24
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:18.584
Your turn. Say: Doesn't have to.

25
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:22.713
Doesn't have to.

26
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.509
Obligation.

27
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:27.899
Obligation means something you must do.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:30.227
Homework is an obligation.

29
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:33.411
Your turn. Say: Obligation.

30
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:37.454
Obligation.

31
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:39.496
No obligation.

32
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:43.133
No obligation means nothing that you must do.

33
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:45.287
There is no obligation.

34
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:48.710
Your turn. Say: No obligation.

35
00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.230
No obligation.

36
00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:54.729
Rule.

37
00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:58.808
Rule means a statement about what you must or must not do.

38
00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.196
School has many rules.

39
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:04.726
Your turn. Say: Rule.

40
00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:08.463
Rule.

41
00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:10.334
Necessary.

42
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:14.220
Necessary means needed; you cannot avoid it.

43
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:16.596
A ticket is necessary.

44
00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:19.870
Your turn. Say: Necessary.

45
00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:23.897
Necessary.

46
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.293
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.823
Visal, what do you have to do at school every day?

48
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:42.387
I have to arrive before eight and I have to wear a uniform. Have to expresses obligation from a rule. With he, she and it we say has to.

49
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:44.810
And don't have to?

50
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:56.748
It means it is not necessary. I don't have to wear a uniform on Saturday. We can choose, but we are allowed to do it. Don't have to is not the same as must not.

51
00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.408
How do we make questions?

52
00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:11.524
Do you have to wear a uniform? Does she have to work? We answer Yes, I do or No, I don't. After have to, always use the base verb. In the past we say had to.

53
00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.167
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.017 --> 00:03:19.745
Grammar focus: Obligation: have to and has to and don't have to.

55
00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:21.324
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:23.575
I have to wear a uniform.

57
00:03:24.483 --> 00:03:26.088
She has to get up early.

58
00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:28.774
You don't have to pay for the ticket.

59
00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:38.713
Have to / has to = obligation; don't have to / doesn't have to = not necessary. Questions: Do you have to…? After have to, use the base verb.

60
00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.170
Be careful! Don't say: She have to go home now.

61
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.388
Say: She has to go home now.

62
00:03:47.688 --> 00:03:49.189
Use has to with she.

63
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.652
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:54.932
Rules and Choices.

65
00:03:55.232 --> 00:03:59.205
At school, I have to wear a uniform and I have to arrive before eight.

66
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.548
My sister has to get up at five o'clock.

67
00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:05.893
On Saturday, we don't have to go to school.

68
00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.540
Do you have to work on Sunday?

69
00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:11.730
A rule is something that you must follow.

70
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:17.183
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.585
She blank to get up early.

72
00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:23.051
A, have. B, has. C, having.

73
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.785
The answer is B: has.

74
00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.066
On Sunday we blank go to school.

75
00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:36.147
A, don't have to. B, must not. C, has to.

76
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.630
The answer is A: don't have to.

77
00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:44.818
blank you have to wear a uniform?

78
00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:48.609
A, Do. B, Are. C, Must.

79
00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.876
The answer is A: Do.

80
00:04:55.017 --> 00:04:56.587
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:56.887 --> 00:05:01.666
A, She has to goes.. B, She has to go.. C, She have to go..

82
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.385
The answer is B: She has to go..

83
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.130
According to the reading, who gets up at five?

84
00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:15.362
A, my sister. B, my father. C, my friend.

85
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.760
The answer is A: my sister.

86
00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:24.979
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:25.817 --> 00:05:29.003
What do you have to do at school? What don't you have to do?

88
00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:39.375
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:39.675 --> 00:05:52.036
At school, I have to wear a uniform and I have to be quiet in the library. I don't have to bring lunch because there is a canteen. I use have to for obligation and don't have to when it is not necessary.

90
00:05:52.336 --> 00:05:53.999
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.883 --> 00:06:00.682
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and obligation: have to and has to and don't have to.

92
00:06:00.982 --> 00:06:05.236
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

93
00:06:05.536 --> 00:06:08.142
See you in Unit thirty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.442 --> 00:06:11.269
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

